From: leopard-webkit-build
Subject: [PATCH] gstreamer: gate GstStream/Converter (1.6/1.10+) behind GST_CHECK_VERSION

WebKit 610's GStreamer code unconditionally references four type families
that don't exist in GStreamer 1.4.5 (the version we bundle in the app for
10.6 compatibility):

  - GstStream, GstStreamCollection (1.10 stable)
  - GstVideoConverter, GstAudioConverter (1.6)

The references live in template specializations in GRefPtrGStreamer.{h,cpp}
and GUniquePtrGStreamer.h, and propagate into the public signatures of
~7 consumer files (MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer, TrackPrivateBaseGStreamer,
and the Audio/Video/InbandTextTrackPrivateGStreamer subclasses).

The GstStream code path is driven by GST_MESSAGE_STREAMS_SELECTED, which
is playbin3-only. This build selects playbin at runtime (m_isLegacyPlaybin
= TRUE), so the entire streams-selected path is runtime-dead. The link
must still resolve, however, so this patch gates the specializations and
all call sites behind GST_CHECK_VERSION(1,10,0) (and the converter
deleters behind GST_CHECK_VERSION(1,6,0)).

NB: This patch gates the *playbin3* path only. It does NOT touch the
USE(GSTREAMER_GL) guard, which is a separate (currently broken — see
spikes/gstreamer-webkit-header-floor/README.md) concern. When USE_GSTREAMER_GL
is genuinely ON at compile time, additional gating will be needed for the
GL/EGL-on-Cocoa path; capture that as a follow-up patch then.

See spikes/gstreamer-webkit-header-floor/README.md for the full audit.

---
diff --git a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/GRefPtrGStreamer.h b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/GRefPtrGStreamer.h
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/GRefPtrGStreamer.h
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/GRefPtrGStreamer.h
@@ -116,6 +116,12 @@
 template<> WebKitWebSrc* refGPtr<WebKitWebSrc>(WebKitWebSrc* ptr);
 template<> void derefGPtr<WebKitWebSrc>(WebKitWebSrc* ptr);
 
+// [leopard] GstStream + GstStreamCollection are 1.10+ APIs. WebKit 610's
+// playbin3 path uses them, but this build runs against the bundled 1.4.5
+// framework and selects playbin at runtime (m_isLegacyPlaybin=TRUE), so the
+// entire streams-selected code path is dead. Gate the specializations out
+// at <1.10 to keep the build linkable against the 1.4.5 dylibs.
+#if GST_CHECK_VERSION(1,10,0)
 template<> GRefPtr<GstStream> adoptGRef(GstStream*);
 template<> GstStream* refGPtr<GstStream>(GstStream*);
 template<> void derefGPtr<GstStream>(GstStream*);
@@ -123,6 +129,7 @@
 template<> GRefPtr<GstStreamCollection> adoptGRef(GstStreamCollection*);
 template<> GstStreamCollection* refGPtr<GstStreamCollection>(GstStreamCollection*);
 template<> void derefGPtr<GstStreamCollection>(GstStreamCollection*);
+#endif
 
 #if USE(GSTREAMER_GL)
 template<> GRefPtr<GstGLDisplay> adoptGRef(GstGLDisplay* ptr);
diff --git a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/GRefPtrGStreamer.cpp b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/GRefPtrGStreamer.cpp
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/GRefPtrGStreamer.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/GRefPtrGStreamer.cpp
@@ -378,6 +378,9 @@
         gst_query_unref(ptr);
 }
 
+// [leopard] GstStream + GstStreamCollection template defs gated to match
+// the corresponding specializations in GRefPtrGStreamer.h. See comment there.
+#if GST_CHECK_VERSION(1,10,0)
 template <> GRefPtr<GstStream> adoptGRef(GstStream* ptr)
 {
     return GRefPtr<GstStream>(ptr, GRefPtrAdopt);
@@ -415,6 +418,7 @@
     if (ptr)
         gst_object_unref(ptr);
 }
+#endif
 
 template <> GRefPtr<WebKitVideoSink> adoptGRef(WebKitVideoSink* ptr)
 {
diff --git a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/GUniquePtrGStreamer.h b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/GUniquePtrGStreamer.h
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/GUniquePtrGStreamer.h
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/GUniquePtrGStreamer.h
@@ -42,8 +42,14 @@
 WTF_DEFINE_GPTR_DELETER(GstSegment, gst_segment_free)
 WTF_DEFINE_GPTR_DELETER(GstFlowCombiner, gst_flow_combiner_free)
 WTF_DEFINE_GPTR_DELETER(GstByteReader, gst_byte_reader_free)
+// [leopard] GstVideoConverter + GstAudioConverter are 1.6+ APIs. No WebKit
+// 610 code path creates a GUniquePtr<GstVideoConverter> / <GstAudioConverter>
+// (verified via grep of platform/graphics/gstreamer/), so gating the
+// deleters off at <1.6 has zero behavior impact.
+#if GST_CHECK_VERSION(1,6,0)
 WTF_DEFINE_GPTR_DELETER(GstVideoConverter, gst_video_converter_free)
 WTF_DEFINE_GPTR_DELETER(GstAudioConverter, gst_audio_converter_free)
+#endif
 
 #if USE(WPE_VIDEO_PLANE_DISPLAY_DMABUF)
 WTF_DEFINE_GPTR_DELETER(struct wpe_video_plane_display_dmabuf_source, wpe_video_plane_display_dmabuf_source_destroy)
